From: Dominik Krivohlavek <github@xkrivo.net>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 19:17:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/31] fix(midea): tolerate all firmware mop drying modes

The firmware accepts mop drying modes 0-7 (6h, 3h, 1h, 100min, 3h, 2h,
3h, 6h; modes 0, 4 and 7 use drying method 2, which is probably
unheated). The getter used to throw for modes 0-4, e.g. when the vendor
app or the default had selected one of them.

Map the modes to the closest existing preset: 0, 4 and 7 to cold, 1 and
6 to 3h, 2, 3 and 5 to 2h. The setter and the offered presets are
unchanged.

Based on static analysis; untested. The table is confirmed, the meaning
of method 2 is likely.

diff --git a/backend/lib/robots/midea/capabilities/MideaMopDockMopDryingTimeControlCapability.js b/backend/lib/robots/midea/capabilities/MideaMopDockMopDryingTimeControlCapability.js
index 68bda489..4979f4f2 100644
--- a/backend/lib/robots/midea/capabilities/MideaMopDockMopDryingTimeControlCapability.js
+++ b/backend/lib/robots/midea/capabilities/MideaMopDockMopDryingTimeControlCapability.js
@@ -19,12 +19,17 @@ class MideaMopDockMopDryingTimeControlCapability extends MopDockMopDryingTimeCon
 
         if (parsedResponse instanceof MSmartMopDockDryingSettingsDTO) {
             switch (parsedResponse.mode) {
-                case 5:
-                    return MideaMopDockMopDryingTimeControlCapability.DURATION.TWO_HOURS;
-                case 6:
-                    return MideaMopDockMopDryingTimeControlCapability.DURATION.THREE_HOURS;
+                case 0:
+                case 4:
                 case 7:
                     return MideaMopDockMopDryingTimeControlCapability.DURATION.COLD;
+                case 1:
+                case 6:
+                    return MideaMopDockMopDryingTimeControlCapability.DURATION.THREE_HOURS;
+                case 2:
+                case 3:
+                case 5:
+                    return MideaMopDockMopDryingTimeControlCapability.DURATION.TWO_HOURS;
                 default:
                     throw new Error(`Received invalid value ${parsedResponse.mode}`);
             }
